@* What a page run under ExGrid.MudBlazor's Chrome (DemoChrome) needs for MudBlazor's own controls
   to render: its stylesheet, and its theme, popover and dialog providers. A page that stands its
   grids on the Wrapper's paper also takes the Wrapper's stylesheet, which maps the grid's Visual
   Tokens onto the palette (ADR-0030), and the font the paper's widths were measured for. A page of
   Sheets takes ExSheet.MudBlazor's stylesheet, which lays out Format Cells' dialog (ADR-0063). Under
   the core's Chrome nothing here renders, and the page is what it always was. *@
@* A page asked for the dark scheme (DemoChrome.IsDark) declares it for the whole document, as a host
   page in dark mode does: the core's defaults on system colours follow it (ADR-0027), and MudBlazor
   paints its dark palette. One HeadContent, because a page shows only the last one rendered. *@
@using global::MudBlazor

@if (DemoChrome.IsMud(Name) || Dark)
{
    <HeadContent>
        @if (Dark)
        {
            <style>:root { color-scheme: dark; }</style>
        }
        @if (DemoChrome.IsMud(Name))
        {
            @if (Paper)
            {
                <link href="_content/ExGrid.DemoPages/fonts/roboto/roboto.css" rel="stylesheet" />
            }
            <link href="_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
            @if (Paper)
            {
                <link href="_content/ExGrid.MudBlazor/mud-ex-grid.css" rel="stylesheet" />
            }
            @if (Sheet)
            {
                <link href="_content/ExSheet.MudBlazor/mud-ex-sheet.css" rel="stylesheet" />
            }
        }
    </HeadContent>
}
@if (DemoChrome.IsMud(Name))
{
    <MudThemeProvider IsDarkMode="Dark" />
    <MudPopoverProvider />
    <MudDialogProvider />
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The page's <c>?chrome=</c> value.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Name { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the page stands its grids on the Wrapper's paper under the Wrapper's
    /// Chrome.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Paper { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the page shows Sheets, whose Format Cells is ExSheet.MudBlazor's dialog
    /// under the Wrapper's Chrome.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Sheet { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the page is shown in the dark scheme (<see cref="DemoChrome.IsDark"/>).</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Dark { get; set; }
}
